  "summary_en": "European Parliamentary Research Service briefing on the Commission's Digital Omnibus on AI proposal (COM(2025) 836), which amends the AI Act and the civil aviation Regulation 2018/1139 to simplify implementation, delay high-risk rules, and ease burdens. It covers legislative progress, stakeholder views, and the June 2026 parliamentary approval of the trilogue agreement.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "High-risk AI rules' application is tied to availability of standards, with backstops of 2 Dec 2027 (Annex III) and 2 Aug 2028 (Annex I).",
   "AI Office centralises enforcement for AI in very large platforms and for GPAI-based systems from the same provider.",
   "AI literacy obligation replaced by a duty on the Commission and Member States to promote it.",
   "SME simplifications extended to small mid-caps; sandboxes expanded, including an EU-level sandbox.",
   "Special-category personal data may be processed for bias detection; the interplay with civil aviation rules and GDPR is clarified."
  ],
